note right of SprintsPage
ProjectLayoutPage child. SprintListView.refresh =
layout.revision() + refreshCount(). Registers Plan sprint
with layout.setTabAction({ label, run: openPlanSprint })
while pausedChange is false; clears it (null) in Kanban
mode and on destroy. planRequested calls openPlanSprint;
editRequested, startRequested, scopeRequested and
closeRequested carry the sprint ID to the open method.
Dialogs get workspaceName from layout.workspace();
scope and close dialogs get offerSprintsLink = false.
SprintFormOutcome: Saved after Plan sprint -> open the
new sprint's plan; Saved after Edit -> refreshCount + 1
and "Changes saved" toast; ModeChanged ->
layout.modeChanged(); Outdated -> refreshCount + 1.
StartSprintOutcome: Started -> open the board with the
"Sprint 9 started" toast; ModeChanged -> modeChanged();
Outdated -> refreshCount + 1; CloseSprint(sprint) ->
openCloseSprint(sprint.sprintId).
SprintScopeOutcome: Changed -> refreshCount + 1 and
"Scope updated" toast with its summary; Outdated ->
refreshCount + 1.
CloseSprintOutcome: Closed -> open its history with the
"Sprint 8 closed" toast; Outdated -> refreshCount + 1.
While a dialog is open: unconfirmed -> refreshCount + 1
at once; forbidden -> "Your access changed" toast,
without Retry.
Toasts go through TOAST_SERVICE.
changeModeRequested calls layout.openDialog(ChangeMode);
retryRequested and the first notFound call
layout.refresh(), so header and list reread together.
draft delegates to the open dialog, else to
inject(ProjectLayoutPage).draft(), since the layout
route has no canDeactivate; UnsavedChangesGuard is
the sprints route's canDeactivate.
end note
