note right of SprintForm
  Edit: sprint = sprintPlanResource(...) for the plan
  header; the draft starts from the first resolved value,
  the fields stay disabled until then, and a failed read
  keeps them disabled with Try again = sprint.reload().
  A stale 409 calls sprint.reload() once. A sprints-paused
  409 keeps the draft, disables Save and emits modeChanged;
  a not-planned 409 does the same and emits outdated.
  A read or save 404 emits notFound; an unexpected
  403 keeps the draft and emits forbidden.
  No response: keep the draft; "We couldn't confirm
  whether ..."; emit unconfirmed. Edit reloads the
  sprint once: a newer version shows the comparison
  under "The latest saved version is shown beside your
  entries". Plan sprint: Save stays unavailable.
  Plan sprint: query undefined, nothing is read.
end note
