note bottom of SprintPlanView
Renders the header actions: Edit details and Start sprint
emit editRequested and startRequested with sprintId, both
disabled while paused, not planned, or a save is pending.
A refresh change rereads the header and both lists and
keeps toAdd and toRemove.
preMarkedRemoval reads its member row once (member query
storyId) and seeds toRemove, as Remove would, only when that
read returns it as a current member; otherwise nothing is marked.
preMarkedAddition reads its candidate row once (query storyId)
and seeds toAdd when the story is eligible. A save 400 naming
a story to remove as not a member drops that mark and names it
("HCK-126 is no longer in Sprint 9, so it isn't removed").
draftChange is dirty while either set is non-empty
("2 to add - 1 to remove").
The header's mode and status decide the read-only paused
view (Kanban) and the not-planned explanation; after a save
with no response, a header no longer Planned shows only its
state ("Sprint 9 is active now.", unconfirmed-active).
An unexpected 403 on Save plan keeps both sets and
emits forbidden.
end note
